            <ArticleTitle>In vitro and in vivo evaluation of O-alkyl derivatives of tramadol.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1674-80</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.bmcl.2008.01.051</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Tramadol is a centrally acting opioid analgesic structurally related to codeine and morphine. O-Alkyl, N-desmethyl, and non-phenol containing derivatives of tramadol were synthesized to probe their effect on metabolic stability and both in vitro and in vivo potency.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
